  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>ADCHeader</name>
    <text>ADC</text>
    <x>18</x>
    <y>65</y>
    <width>70</width>
    <height>28</height>
    <font>
      <font family="Liberation Sans" style="BOLD" size="18.0">
      </font>
    </font>
  </widget>
  <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
    <name>ADCValue</name>
    <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):ADC_100MS</pv_name>
    <x>150</x>
    <y>62</y>
    <width>170</width>
    <height>34</height>
    <format>3</format>
    <precision>6</precision>
    <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    <vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment>
    <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):ADC_100MS (CH$(CH)_ADC_100MS)

ADC integral of channel $(CH) averaged over the last 100 ms, in calibrated
units. This is the value the interlock compares against the ADC thresholds.</tooltip>
    <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
  </widget>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>FBRHeader</name>
    <text>FBR</text>
    <x>350</x>
    <y>65</y>
    <width>70</width>
    <height>28</height>
    <font>
      <font family="Liberation Sans" style="BOLD" size="18.0">
      </font>
    </font>
  </widget>
  <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
    <name>FBRValue</name>
    <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):FBR_CNT_100MS</pv_name>
    <x>480</x>
    <y>62</y>
    <width>170</width>
    <height>34</height>
    <format>3</format>
    <precision>6</precision>
    <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    <vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment>
    <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):FBR_CNT_100MS (CH$(CH)_FBR_CNT_100MS)

Fiber count of channel $(CH) accumulated over the last 100 ms. This is the
value the interlock compares against the FBR thresholds.</tooltip>
    <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
  </widget>
  <widget type="textentry" version="3.0.0">
    <name>ADCFilter</name>
    <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):ADC_FILT_TH</pv_name>
    <x>710</x>
    <y>62</y>
    <width>180</width>
    <height>34</height>
    <show_units>true</show_units>
    <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):ADC_FILT_TH (ADC_FILT_TH_CH$(CH))

ADC filter threshold of channel $(CH), in calibrated units. Samples below
this level are dropped before the integrals are formed, which keeps noise from
accumulating into the longer time scales. The value is converted to raw ADC
counts with the inverse calibration before it is written to the FPGA.</tooltip>
  </widget>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>ADCFilterLabel</name>
    <text>ADC filter threshold</text>
    <x>710</x>
    <y>98</y>
    <width>180</width>
    <height>22</height>
    <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
  </widget>
  <widget type="textentry" version="3.0.0">
    <name>DACSP</name>
    <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):DAC_REF_SP</pv_name>
    <x>910</x>
    <y>62</y>
    <width>120</width>
    <height>34</height>
    <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):DAC_REF_SP (DAC_REF_CH$(CH))

Comparator reference voltage of channel $(CH) in mV, valid range 0 to 2500 mV.
It is written to the matching DAC80508 output over SPI as soon as the value
changes, and sets the analog threshold the FPGA compares the input against.</tooltip>
  </widget>
  <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
    <name>DACRBV</name>
    <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):DAC_REF_RBV</pv_name>
    <x>1040</x>
    <y>62</y>
    <width>120</width>
    <height>34</height>
    <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    <vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment>
    <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):DAC_REF_RBV (DAC_REF_CH$(CH)_RB)

Reference voltage of channel $(CH) read back from the DAC80508, in mV. It
follows the setpoint within one status poll interval; a persistent mismatch
means the DAC did not accept the write.</tooltip>
    <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
  </widget>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>DACSPLabel</name>
    <text>DAC setpoint (mV)</text>
    <x>910</x>
    <y>98</y>
    <width>120</width>
    <height>22</height>
    <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
  </widget>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>DACRBVLabel</name>
    <text>DAC readback (mV)</text>
    <x>1040</x>
    <y>98</y>
    <width>120</width>
    <height>22</height>
    <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
  </widget>
  <widget type="group" version="3.0.0">
    <name>Thresholds</name>
